WEBVTT

00:00:00.320 --> 00:00:27.820
<v Tim / GM>Last time on Cloudfall. It's dunker day aboard the heavenly feather, but something felt off at the dinner table. Rolan was acting incredibly suspicious and prompted a private meeting in the cargo hold. It turns out the party was being surveilled by Libera with a hidden echo bell, but it also turns out that Rolan is a good guy and told them the truth. Now the Isle of Lor is just moments away, and there's no telling what awaits them in the clouds.

00:01:24.515 --> 00:01:45.375
<v Tim / GM>It is still early morning aboard the heavenly feather. Poppy got up real early to start baking all of her cookies, and people have begun to notice. Yarhar came by just a moment ago for a early morning stop to let you know that Lor would be approaching in the distance in, an hour or so, But, Poppy, you've got a line outside the wagon.

00:01:47.195 --> 00:01:51.790
<v Maggie / Poppy>Sorry. I think, canonically, Poppy wakes up with a voice like

00:01:52.430 --> 00:01:52.930
<v Tim / GM>Yeah.

00:01:54.830 --> 00:01:59.355
<v Maggie / Poppy>Oh, wait. Good morning, everyone. Single file line, please.

00:01:59.655 --> 00:02:04.875
<v Tim / GM>There's, like, a whole, like, lumped crowd around the wagon that immediately shapes up into a single file.

00:02:04.990 --> 00:02:08.370
<v Maggie / Poppy>It's 1 at a time and don't ruin your breakfast.

00:02:09.470 --> 00:02:17.445
<v Tim / GM>The first person who comes up is offering to pay with gold. They put 2 gold coins on the counter of the window that looks outside from the wagon. They say,

00:02:18.065 --> 00:02:20.005
<v Tim / GM>how money do I get for 2 gold?

00:02:20.545 --> 00:02:23.820
<v Maggie / Poppy>I'm running a deal where you can get 10 cookies for that much.

00:02:24.200 --> 00:02:27.400
<v Tim / GM>He looks behind him and all of his friends and they all get super excited and

00:02:27.400 --> 00:02:28.620
<v Tim / GM>he goes, I'll take 20.

00:02:29.160 --> 00:02:33.965
<v Maggie / Poppy>Oh, perfect. Yes. Just let me wrap them up for you. Hold on.

00:02:34.425 --> 00:02:43.550
<v Tim / GM>People behind them are eagerly, pushing forward. It seems there's some concern about which flavor is going to run out first. What is your protocol for this?

00:02:44.010 --> 00:02:46.935
<v Maggie / Poppy>Well, when we run out, we run out. I'm a small business.

00:02:47.795 --> 00:02:50.135
<v Tim / GM>You hear some unhappy rumblings.

00:02:50.835 --> 00:02:54.375
<v Maggie / Poppy>Every cookie is just as good as the last. That's my puppy guarantee.

00:02:54.915 --> 00:03:00.180
<v Tim / GM>Guy, what is your position in this case? When when the go in is good and cookies are selling like

00:03:02.740 --> 00:03:04.680
<v Maggie / Poppy>I do have hotcakes, actually.

00:03:04.740 --> 00:03:05.240
<v Tim / GM>Okay.

00:03:07.045 --> 00:03:09.945
<v Thomas / Guy>Guy is not taking money at the counter.

00:03:10.405 --> 00:03:23.240
<v Tim / GM>Here's the thing. If Poppy's gotta work the window, somebody's gotta be doing the ovens. Somebody's gotta be moving sheets back and forth, but more importantly, somebody's gotta be watching to make sure that things don't burn. Yep. Guy, how do you accomplish both of these things at the same time?

00:03:23.685 --> 00:03:42.855
<v Thomas / Guy>Wow. Boy. It's like I would need 2 sets of eyes or something. Guy's head is positioned on the counter across from the oven k. Down low so it can see through the window of the oven to make sure nothing's burning.

00:03:42.855 --> 00:03:51.950
<v Thomas / Guy>And then the body is moving trays around, taking the cookies off the trays, and, moving product.

00:03:52.410 --> 00:04:01.135
<v Tim / GM>So crucial question going forward. Can your head get around by any means, and can your body understand what it's doing without the head?

00:04:01.675 --> 00:04:09.750
<v Thomas / Guy>The head does not have its own locomotion. So as long as the head can see the body, the body knows what it's doing.

00:04:09.750 --> 00:04:20.775
<v Tim / GM>Got it. Okay. Easy rule to follow. The rest of you can see what's going on here. Most of the crew is on the main deck kind of crowding around, the Rolling Pin.

00:04:21.250 --> 00:04:26.630
<v Tim / GM>Journey, you had come down from the rigging a little while ago. What is your reaction to seeing so many people crowded around?

00:04:27.970 --> 00:04:28.370
<v Tara / Journey>I'm kind

00:04:28.370 --> 00:04:59.150
<v Tara / Journey>of enraptured by it, honestly. Like, Journey had experienced city life a little bit, had seen the crowds for the airship festival, but had seen them kind of from afar. This is someone she knows being surrounded by people that she doesn't really know, but she doesn't have any reason to distrust. And everyone's pretty chipper and jovial. So she's just kinda like, oh, this is this is what it looks like when people are all gathered together.

00:04:59.150 --> 00:05:05.325
<v Tara / Journey>When they all live in one big place together, then they do this sometimes and it's fun.

00:05:06.025 --> 00:05:17.940
<v Tim / GM>Yeah. It might be a little different from what you saw in Farewell. A lot of people in Farewell are trying to do the best for themselves. Mhmm. And this might be the first time that you've seen a real community outside of your own.

00:05:18.480 --> 00:05:28.245
<v Tara / Journey>I think that that would occur to Journey. Like, this is functioning kind of the way her family functions at home. Yeah. Everybody has something that they're doing.

00:05:28.860 --> 00:05:31.180
