<v Tim / GM>passage. I did not.

00:12:31.640 --> 00:12:32.620
<v Maggie / Poppy>It's not free?

00:12:33.880 --> 00:12:35.980
<v Tim / GM>You're not paying, but it wasn't free.

00:12:36.505 --> 00:12:39.545
<v Maggie / Poppy>Oh, cool. Just racking up that.

00:12:39.545 --> 00:12:41.785
<v Tara / Journey>That's just

00:12:41.785 --> 00:12:42.905
<v Maggie / Poppy>make a mental note.

00:12:42.905 --> 00:12:54.425
<v Tim / GM>Well, hopefully, this clears your mind a little bit. Seems you made a good impression. This is a gift. Chef Bowie is cleaning up breakfast right now, but they wanted me to give you this. What?

00:12:54.485 --> 00:12:56.745
<v Tim / GM>He hands you a, pewter ladle.

00:12:57.445 --> 00:12:59.785
<v Maggie / Poppy>Okay. What, thank you?

00:13:00.165 --> 00:13:01.820
<v Tim / GM>Yeah. Well, Bowie told

00:13:01.820 --> 00:13:04.240
<v Tim / GM>me that, you're magically inclined.

00:13:04.540 --> 00:13:05.360
<v Tim / GM>Is that true?

00:13:05.660 --> 00:13:06.480
<v Maggie / Poppy>That's correct.

00:13:09.180 --> 00:13:09.775
<v Tim / GM>They also told me

00:13:09.775 --> 00:13:24.930
<v Tim / GM>what a big help you were. This is one of their old favorite ladles, but we used to work in bars, and they would use it to fend off, unruly drunken magic users, so well, basically, you can catch small spells in this and whip it back at people.

00:13:25.070 --> 00:13:35.800
<v Maggie / Poppy>Fuck yes. I have to write that down. Wow. I mean, that's pretty cool. I've never seen one of these before.

00:13:35.880 --> 00:13:39.740
<v Maggie / Poppy>Well, I mean, I've seen a ladle before, but I've never used it for that.

00:13:40.040 --> 00:13:41.320
<v Tim / GM>He goes, yeah. It is

00:13:41.320 --> 00:13:44.755
<v Tim / GM>a nice gift, isn't it? Yeah. I hope it serves you well.

00:13:44.815 --> 00:13:45.635
<v Maggie / Poppy>Thank you.

00:13:46.335 --> 00:13:50.355
